@@ -15,3 +15,30 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Agent tools
+
+The hydrated authentication forms expose WebMCP tools to compatible browser agents:
+
+| Page | Tool | Inputs | Action |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| `/signin` | `sign_in` | `username`, `password` (non-empty strings) | Submit the existing login request. |
+| `/signup` | `sign_up` | `username`, `password` (non-empty strings) | Register an account; does not sign in. The server enforces password requirements. |
+
+Tools are registered while their form is mounted using `document.modelContext`,
+with compatibility for older `navigator.modelContext` previews. Browsers without
+WebMCP keep the ordinary forms. No MCP server or additional service is required.
+The implementation follows the [WebMCP imperative API](https://developer.chrome.com/docs/modern-web-guidance/guides/webmcp/agentic-javascript-tools).
+
+Agent submissions share the manual forms' validation, loading state, API calls,
+and visible success/error messages. Each call returns a text content block
+containing JSON `{ success, message }` and sets `isError` on failure. Results do
+not include passwords or API tokens. Concurrent submissions are rejected; tool
+cancellation and component unmount cancel in-flight requests. Registration is
+removed when the form unmounts.
+
+Run the non-browser tool checks with Node 24:
+
+```sh
+node --experimental-strip-types --test tests/auth-tools.test.ts
+```
